2. Substantial reuse

Substantial reuse means redistributing the project as a whole, including
a fork or port, or incorporating or adapting its original implementation
of a meaningful user-facing feature. Functionality, rather than a line
count or percentage of your code, determines this.

Isolated lines, incidental helpers, standard programming constructs and
API calls require no reward share or additional public credit. Source
credit is appreciated where appropriate.

3. CurseForge Reward Points

If such a derivative project earns CurseForge Reward Points, allocate
at least 10% of that project's points to antrakt92 through CurseForge's
Members reward allocation. Maintain the share while it uses the covered
work and earns points. A single 10% share to antrakt92 per derivative
project satisfies the reward-sharing requirement for all Antrakt/Antrakt92
projects reused in it. Reusing several source projects does not increase
the required share. Each separate derivative project is assessed separately.
The share concerns that derivative project only, not account earnings,
other projects, donations or other revenue. No points earned means no payment.

Send the member invitation required by CurseForge and enable the required
share when it is accepted and the platform permits it. A pending invitation
awaiting the author's acceptance does not by itself breach this condition.
No separate permission request or negotiated agreement is needed.
CurseForge's own rules still apply.

4. Uses that require no share

Installation, gameplay, recommendations, links, dependency references and
collections that reference the original download require no reward share.
Independently written implementations, translations and compatibility
patches also require no reward share or additional public credit unless
they substantially reuse the covered implementation.

